# Recoder — Open Work (not-done only)

Outstanding work only. Shipped history lives in git + closed `bd` issues — not here.
Source-of-truth order: plan.md → remaining.md → prd.md/product.md → this file.

## Paid-user launch gate (blocks first paid users)

- GitHub delivery: PR webhook ingestion now links Agent OS delivery records to GitHub issues referenced from PR bodies (`Fixes #123` / issue URLs), and `pnpm --dir docker-backend run agent-os:verify-paid-loop` now exercises PR + preview delivery-link records; still needs deployed adapter/webhook verification against the production PR-artifact flow.
- Task timeline: `pnpm --dir docker-backend run agent-os:verify-paid-loop` verifies `task → instruction bundle → runtime event/evidence → artifact → PR → preview → approval → history/outbox` over Agent OS APIs, and the Agent OS UI now renders run, delivery, runtime-evidence, and approval cards from `/api/agent-os/summary`; still needs deployed UI/API verification against real paid-user data.
- CloudEvent outbox: production env gates now require `NATS_URL` plus Agent OS outbox drain enablement, and `pnpm --dir docker-backend run agent-os:verify-outbox-nats` verifies pending outbox drain against JetStream; still needs that verifier run on the deployed stack with real pending records.
- Instruction provenance: paid-loop verifier now compiles and stores InstructionBundle artifacts through deployed Agent OS APIs, and the Agent OS UI renders durable instruction artifact metadata from `/api/agent-os/summary`; still needs deployed UI verification of compiled InstructionBundle artifacts.
- Runtime evidence: `/api/agent-os/events` now projects embedded runtime-adapter `runtimeEvidence` / `runtimeEvidenceItems` payloads into durable RuntimeEvidence records and outbox events, and the paid-loop verifier checks that projection; still needs deployed runtime-adapter coverage for real sandbox sessions across every paid-user runtime.
- MCP approval loop: local Agent OS regression and the paid-loop verifier now prove `needs_approval` policy decisions materialize pending approvals and approve/reject decisions emit approval outbox events; still needs deployed PM verification against real MCP tool calls.
- Live edge/preview rollout: DNS, TLS, protected preview hosts, rate limits, WAF hooks, production verification (`recoder-zvss`).
- Hetzner deploy hygiene: reconcile local↔prod git divergence so full deploys don't need scoped checkout/build handling (`recoder-js56`).
- Production traffic/abuse controls: rate-limit abuse now flows into admin alerts locally; still needs real-traffic threshold tuning + production alert review (`recoder-a9rp`, `recoder-rbc2`).

## Security / hardening

- [recoder-0zso] `/api/a2a/*` auth — `authenticateRequest` now accepts trusted product-service calls via `x-internal-service-key` / bearer `INTERNAL_SERVICE_KEY`, and the legacy A2A task/orchestration mounts now require auth for mutating methods while preserving GET/HEAD/OPTIONS discovery/read compatibility. Still needs full product-loop runtime verification before broadening enforcement further. `.well-known/agent.json` stays public by spec.

## Capability layer — follow-ups (prod, infra access required)

- Bring up Qdrant + ziti on prod (NOT Ollama/vLLM — 16GB/no-GPU box); set cloud LLM + Gemini keys per `docker-backend/.env.capabilities.recoder-server`.
- Stand up OpenZiti controller end-to-end + provision a runner (`scripts/provision-ziti-runner.sh`); needs CA trust (`NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`).
- Free prod disk before enabling capability backends. As of 2026-06-19: **83% used / 25G free** after stopping the idle Daytona stack + meilisearch/hatchet/openmeter/umami and removing their images. NOTE: the old "135GB is vcpeer" claim is **wrong** — vcpeer is ~42GB (`/opt/vcpeer` 40G + `/root/vcpeer` 1.6G); still do not touch it. The real hogs were `docker/overlay2` (~48G) and the `/root/recoder.xyz` build tree (18G). Remaining optional reclaim: ~2G of unused Daytona data volumes (`docker volume prune` — destroys daytona db/registry state, confirm first).

